  "named": "Measured from the stub's log: the block menu's Copy Properties > Transforms and the Design panel's More actions > Copy transforms each call navigator.clipboard.writeText in the top window, and both Pastes call readText, so the oracle keeps this clip in the system clipboard as text. Every call went to the stub, so nothing reached the machine's clipboard. Not read: whether the two share the same text. stubClipboard ran again before each paste and emptied the stub, so both pastes read an empty string and changed nothing (B and Q stayed 0 deg, 100%): a step mistake, not a read."
